evolve doesn't like me hide this  team-focused shooter forces you to face  a grotesque monster in each and every  match and should you find it you can't  always flee here's the setup a  four-person team of hunters each touting  very specific talents is on the prowl  the quarry is a single creature with an  appetite for flesh not just the flesh of  the hunters but for anything that moves  by attacking the wildlife and chomping  down on its meet the monster evolves  through three stages of being each more  powerful than the last  clearly the hunters would rather tear  the monster down with the least  resistance possible so finding the  creature quickly and destroying it is a  good opening goal  Oh weren't that so easy should you join  a team of hunters you rely on a  particular squad mate to lead you to the  beasts that would be the trapper and  while you eventually unlock two other  trappers to choose from  evolve smartly taps Maggie as your  initial leader  Maggie makes for a good guide through  the ins and outs of pursuits because  she's not a lone ranger instead she  relies on her best friend Daisy an  animal called a trap jaw that follows  the monsters tracks and leads you to its  current location with or without Daisy  the hunting phase captures the essence  of a hunt it's tense simmering with a  possibility of a vicious monster attack  at any moment and like a real-life  hunting trip there might be stretches of  boredom a sneaky monster might Crouch to  hide its tracks or double back on its  own path thus leaving a confiding set of  paw prints even with a veteran crew  evolve occasionally tips onto the side  of boredom the good news is that hunts  don't usually hit the boredom breaking  point  there's wildlife to contend with for  starters though you'll ignore most of  the critters impossible yet you can't  always ignore them  either because killing one rewards you  with a temporary buff or because a not  actually a rock comes to life and starts  chomping on your tasty bits the world of  Scheer isn't hospitable though humans  certainly tried to tame  and then the big moment arrives in the  foreshadowed attack occurs battles are  fresh and exciting due to an in-game  conspiracy devised by involves many  variables there are the rising plateaus  that provide vantage points  there's the hunters vast dome which  traps the monster within its confines  and there's the hunters own weapons and  skills which damage and limit the  monster in various ways assault expert  Hyde uses toxic grenades the poison the  monster and help drive it to different  areas support class robot bucket drops  floating turrets that help the monster  with bullets and tracker Abe slows down  the target with stasis grenades these  battles are invariably intense there are  three monsters in total the ground  pounding Goliath the airborne Kraken and  the rate Master of the hit and run  the Lions battle is typically the most  straightforward the brute attacks  head-on throwing boulders and breathing  fire battle with the Kraken plays out  differently as this peculiar beast rises  above you and spits down lightning as  you can guess situational awareness wins  and losses matches as you become more  experienced you learn how to exploit  shears vertical spaces using a jetpack  to float to better locations and putting  obstacles between you and your  flesh-eating stalker there is no room  for a chest thumping Supercenter if  you'd rather be a lone damage dealer  then it's best just to play is the  monster playing as the monster is  deliciously evil particularly when  choosing the Wraith who can swoop in  grab a hunter and rush away depositing  the hunter somewhere else in the  vicinity monstering it up is just as  fulfilling as engaging in the hunt  though the pace is different you spend  the early minutes sniffing out the  wildlife and satiating your hunger which  not only reinforces your shield but also  brings you that much closer to evolving  smart play can yield victory if you go  up to the hunters stage 1 it's best to  avoid the confrontation until you're the  biggest bully you always knew you could  be just as good hunters are constantly  in motion so too is a good monster  the tempo changes considerably when you  abandon the core hunt mode and  experiment with other possibilities  there's nest mode for instance in which  the hunters must gun down a half-dozen  monster eggs ready to be hatched before  the monster annihilates the team monster  in turn can hatch an egg to spawn a  minion which tears through the jungle on  routes of a pack of hunters even at  stage one following a minion into a war  zone is incredibly tempting not only  does a duo do more damage but the  addition of another combatant can  confuse the team of hunters defend mode  meanwhile takes its cues from battle  arenas like League of Legends and dota  tasking hunters with shielding  generators while minions spawn onto the  map as specified intervals and go on the  attack its evolves most action-packed  mode and as such it's an appropriate end  for the game's evacuation mode which  combines five matches of varying types  into a single big match the winner of  each individual match gains a boon for  the next monster targeting turrets might  appear in various nooks for instance  evolve apparently rebalances matches  even as it adds these map gimmicks  so that winning the first match does not  initiate a five-match steamroll even so  it's hard to tell whether the  behind-the-scenes rebalancing properly  matches the gimmick it's profoundly  irritating to deal with those turrets as  a monster for instance because they  might gun down wandering wildlife not  only damaging you if you get too close  but complicating the simple act of  eating not every gameplay variant in  this mode feels as fair as the last  it's worth noting that evolve supports  BOTS which is an all too uncommon  feature and while the AI reveals its  imperfections as time goes on its strong  enough to make playing offline matches  rewarding on its own terms and BOTS will  fill in for disconnected teammates or  will leap into action should you not be  able to find a friend to take that  particular role whether with friends  strangers or AI though it's fun to focus  on evolves unique brand of greatness  suspense of the Hunts the exhilaration  of battle and the drive to dominate  you
 

